<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mohammed III of Morocco</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1710–1790</span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> · Also known as Sidi Mohammed ibn Abdallah, Mohammed ben Abdallah</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Mohammed III of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/morocco">Morocco</a>, known as Sidi Mohammed ibn Abdallah, was Alaouite sultan from 1757 to 1790. He restored order after decades of civil strife, founded the port of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/essaouira">Essaouira</a> (Mogador) to control foreign trade, recaptured <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/el-jadida">Mazagan</a> from the Portuguese in 1769 and signed treaties with European states and, in 1786, with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a>.</p></div>
